{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.FrobeniusSClassification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.FrobeniusSClassification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":49,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.chiRatio_inverts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.chiRatio_inverts","kind":"theorem","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L329-L343","doc":"**`Φ₃` is S-odd on chains of homogeneous factors.** For a chain `Ps`\nof bar-homogeneous factors, `S` inverts the ratio `χ_sym/χ_alt`\n(stated without division), so `log|χ_sym/χ_alt|` changes sign\nunder `S` at every evaluation point where both characters are nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.primitives_barHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.primitives_barHom","kind":"theorem","line":320,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L320-L327","doc":"The three quark primitives `uu = (1,0)`, `dd = (1,−h)`, `ud = (1,−h/2)`\nare homogeneous of sign `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.chi_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.chi_swap","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L309-L318","doc":"**Character swap.** On a homogeneous element of sign `ε`, the bar\ninvolution exchanges the two characters up to the sign `−ε`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.barHom_chainProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.barHom_chainProd","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L299-L307","doc":"Every chain of homogeneous factors is homogeneous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.barHom_hmul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.barHom_hmul","kind":"theorem","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L291-L297","doc":"Homogeneous elements are closed under products, with `ε'' = −ε ε'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.sbar_chainProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.sbar_chainProd","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L284-L289","doc":"Bar of a chain is the chain of the barred factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.sbar_hmul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.sbar_hmul","kind":"theorem","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L278-L282","doc":"The bar involution is multiplicative on two-strand elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.bar_h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.bar_h","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L273-L276","doc":"`σ̄ h = −h` when `σ̄ q = q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.chainProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.chainProd","kind":"def","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L268-L271","doc":"The chain product of a list of two-strand factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.BarHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.BarHom","kind":"def","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L264-L266","doc":"Bar-homogeneity of sign `ε`: `σ̄ c = ε c`, `σ̄ d = −ε d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.sbar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.sbar","kind":"def","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L260-L262","doc":"The bar involution on `c σ + d`: coefficients by `σ̄`, `σ ↦ σ − h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.chiAlt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.chiAlt","kind":"def","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L257-L258","doc":"The alternating character, `σ ↦ −q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.chiSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.chiSym","kind":"def","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L254-L255","doc":"The symmetric character, `σ ↦ q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.hmul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.hmul","kind":"def","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L250-L252","doc":"Product of `a σ + b` and `c σ + d` under `σ² = h σ + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.zC_not_bar_equivariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.zC_not_bar_equivariant","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L221-L225","doc":"**Convention C is not bar-equivariant.** With `q = u²`, `z_C = u/(u²+1)`\nis bar-invariant, but at `u = 2` it violates `z(q⁻¹) = z(q) − h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.bar_equivariant_forces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.bar_equivariant_forces","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L213-L219","doc":"**Converse.** Any weight pair `(z, z')` (values at `q` and `q⁻¹`) for which\nthe trace is bar-equivariant on all elements satisfies `z' = z − h`.  So\nequivariance pins the relation `(*)`; it is not a property of every `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.markov_bar_equivariant_zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.markov_bar_equivariant_zD","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L204-L211","doc":"**Bar-equivariance of the convention-D Markov trace.** For every element\n`c σ + d` (barred coefficients), `tr_q(S(·)) = z_D(q)·c + (d − c h)`\nequals the trace evaluated at `q⁻¹`, `z_D(q⁻¹)·c + d`. Consequently\n`Φ₁(Sβ; q₀) = Φ₁(β; q₀⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.zD_inv_eq_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.zD_inv_eq_sub","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L193-L202","doc":"**`S` exchanges the two loop values.** `z_D(q⁻¹) = z_D(q) − (q − q⁻¹)`,\ni.e. the bar image of `tr σ = z` is `tr σ⁻¹ = z − h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.zD_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.zD_inv","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L184-L191","doc":"**`z_D` at the inverted parameter.** `z_D(q⁻¹) = 1/(q(q²+1))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.zD","kind":"def","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L181-L182","doc":"The canonical (convention D) Markov weight `z_D(q) = q³/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.H_A_squared_is_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.H_A_squared_is_even","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L163-L167","doc":"**Theorem.** The S-eigenvalues of `H_A` and `H_A²` differ:\nH_A is S-odd, H_A² is S-even (square of any eigenvalue type is even). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.s_invariant_ansatz_captures_S_odd_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.s_invariant_ansatz_captures_S_odd_iff","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L146-L159","doc":"**What an S-invariant ansatz can and cannot capture.**  If `V` is\nS-invariant, its S-difference is zero, so it reproduces the mass's\nS-difference at `β` exactly when the two S-odd channels cancel:\n`α·(Φ₁ β − Φ₁(Sβ)) + 2·α·h2·Φ₃ β = 0`.  In particular such an ansatz\nmisses both `Φ₁⁻` and `H_A²·Φ₃`, not only the chirality term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.chirality_sole_S_odd_channel_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.chirality_sole_S_odd_channel_iff","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L132-L144","doc":"**Chirality is the sole S-odd channel iff `α·Φ₁⁻` vanishes.**\nThe S-difference of the mass equals the chirality contribution\n`−2·α·h2·Φ₃ β` exactly when `α·(Φ₁ β − Φ₁(Sβ)) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.mass_S_difference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.mass_S_difference","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L120-L130","doc":"**The S-difference of the mass.**\n`m(Sβ) − m(β) = −α·(Φ₁ β − Φ₁(Sβ)) − 2·α·h2·Φ₃ β`, i.e.\n`−2α(Φ₁⁻ + h²Φ₃)` with `Φ₁⁻ = (Φ₁ − Φ₁∘S)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.massS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.massS","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L116-L118","doc":"The mass functional of the Wedderburn formula, with raw `Φ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.s_symmetric_ansatz_misses_chirality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.s_symmetric_ansatz_misses_chirality","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L94-L103","doc":"**Lemma (S-even tags multiply to S-even).**\nIf α, V_a, V_b are all S-even, then so are α·V_a and α·V_b.  This\nconcerns eigenvalue tags only; for the statement about actual\nfunctionals see `s_invariant_ansatz_captures_S_odd_iff`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.frobenius_s_classification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.frobenius_s_classification","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L79-L92","doc":"**Theorem (term-by-term S-classification, with `Φ₁⁺`).** In the formula\nM = ... + α(1·Φ₁⁺ − 2[3]_q·Φ₂ + H_A²·Φ₃), i.e. with `Φ₁` replaced by its\nS-symmetrised projection (the `Phi_1` field), the three terms have\neigenvalues +1, +1, −1.  This does not apply to the raw `Φ₁`, which has\nno S-eigenvalue; see `mass_S_difference`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:frobenius-s-classification","label":"prop:frobenius-s-classification","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.termEigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.termEigenvalue","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L75-L77","doc":"The S-eigenvalue of a term in the binding correction is the\nproduct of its coefficient and functional eigenvalues. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.Phi_3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.Phi_3","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.Phi_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.Phi_2","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.Phi_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.Phi_1","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L71-L71","doc":"`.even` is the eigenvalue of the Frobenius-symmetrised projection\n`Φ₁⁺ = (Φ₁ + Φ₁∘S)/2`, even by construction.  The raw `Φ₁` used in\nthe mass formula is not an `S`-eigenvector in either convention; under\nD, `S` acts on it as the evaluation flip `q₀ ↦ q₀⁻¹`\n(`markov_bar_equivariant_zD`), and its odd part `Φ₁⁻` is nonzero\n(bean qou-fd2u). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.alpha","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.alpha","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.z","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The Markov weight is NOT an `S`-eigenvector under the canonical\nconvention D, `z = q³/(q²+1)`: `S` sends it to `z − h_A`\n(`zD_inv_eq_sub` below), the other loop value.  The former `.even`\nwas the excised convention-C reading `z = 1/(q^{1/2}+q^{-1/2})`.\n`none` records \"no eigenvalue\"; no declaration reads this field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.H_A2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.H_A2","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.H_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.H_A","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.q3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.q3","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.W_alt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.W_alt","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.W_std","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.W_std","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.W_sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.W_sym","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification.mk","kind":"ctor","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.FrobeniusClassification","kind":"structure","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L47-L73","doc":"The S-classification of each ingredient in the Wedderburn mass\nformula M = ... + α(Φ₁ − 2[3]_q·Φ₂ + H_A²·Φ₃). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.instMulSEigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.instMulSEigenvalue","kind":"instance","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.SEigenvalue.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.SEigenvalue.mul","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L38-L43","doc":"Combine two S-eigenvalues multiplicatively. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.instReprSEigenvalue.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.instReprSEigenvalue.repr","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.instReprSEigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.instReprSEigenvalue","kind":"instance","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.instDecidableEqSEigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.instDecidableEqSEigenvalue","kind":"instance","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.SEigenvalue.odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.SEigenvalue.odd","kind":"ctor","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-s-classification.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.SEigenvalue.even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.SEigenvalue.even","kind":"ctor","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-th